WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:07.260
65, the effects-driven sci-fi movie with lots&nbsp;
of scary dinosaurs, is officially going extinct&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:12.420
at the box office. Stiff competition could be one&nbsp;
reason why, among a whole bunch of other factors.

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:17.700
Starring Adam Driver and Ariana&nbsp;
Greenblatt, 65 is all about Mills,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:23.760
Koa, and their survival on a hostile planet&nbsp;
populated by dinosaurs. These two are the only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:29.040
ones left after their spaceship crashes, and&nbsp;
Mills feels honor-bound to protect the young&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:34.303
Koa. This means 65 is great for people&nbsp;
who like dinosaurs and science-fiction.

00:00:34.303 --> 00:00:36.538
"There's something alien out there."

00:00:36.538 --> 00:00:40.380
Unfortunately, it looks like these people&nbsp;
weren't motivated to go to the movie theaters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:45.360
and 65 has missed the mark in terms of box&nbsp;
office returns. There could be many different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:51.480
reasons why 65 is going extinct, which may include&nbsp;
reviews, competition, and not a lot of star power.

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:58.080
Released on March 10, 2023, 65 has faced&nbsp;
significant competition from several&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:02.433
different movies. A movie like 65 might&nbsp;
already struggle to bring in audiences,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.433 --> 00:01:08.460
but squaring up against the likes of Scream VI&nbsp;
and Creed III hasn't been kind to 65, either.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:15.420
The results have been quite abysmal, with 65&nbsp;
making only $12.3 million at the box office. For&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:22.590
comparison, Scream VI earned a respectable $44.5&nbsp;
million, the franchise's strongest debut yet.

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:27.780
Besides the direct competition from Scream&nbsp;
VI, there are many movies that are still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:32.760
generating income, like Puss in Boots:&nbsp;
The Last Wish, Cocaine Bear, and Avatar:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:37.440
The Way of Water. This means there are plenty of&nbsp;
options when it comes to entertainment, and it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:42.480
seems like 65 didn't generate enough interest to&nbsp;
overpower any of the other choices at the theater.

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:48.720
In addition to stiff competition, the general&nbsp;
critical consensus around 65 has not been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:54.660
favorable. Reviews have not been kind to 65, and&nbsp;
Rotten Tomatoes currently has the movie at a 38%&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.660 --> 00:01:59.520
critical score. However, it seems like the general&nbsp;
audience views the movie in a slightly more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:05.640
positive light, giving the movie a 63% positive&nbsp;
rating. Still, these results are hardly glowing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:10.605
and negative word of mouth can affect box&nbsp;
office yields. Common Sense Media wrote:

00:02:10.605 --> 00:02:13.680
"While this sci-fi/dinosaur&nbsp;
movie is competently made,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:20.040
it really only has one good idea, and it doesn't&nbsp;
do much with it. The rest is generic, familiar,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:22.920
and fails to generate much suspense or emotion."

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:27.900
Not all critics were unkind to the movie. Empire&nbsp;
Magazine thought the movie was bold in creating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:33.960
an original story, noting that the film moved at&nbsp;
a brisk pace, and the no-nonsense plot was buoyed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:39.420
by the occasional Tyrannosaurus Rex. Still,&nbsp;
65 isn't creating a lot of positive chatter.

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:43.440
Another facet to consider is that 65&nbsp;
doesn't have a lot of star power other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:47.700
than Adam Driver. Besides Driver, the&nbsp;
other main star is Ariana Greenblatt,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:52.140
whose biggest claim to fame at this point&nbsp;
is appearing as Young Gamora in Avengers:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:57.420
Infinity War. Driver is not without his army&nbsp;
of dedicated fans, but Driver isn't exactly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.420 --> 00:03:02.880
known as an action star. The one exception to&nbsp;
this is the recent Star Wars sequel trilogy.

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:07.620
Beyond that, however, Driver usually isn't&nbsp;
running and gunning. Perhaps that was the reason&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:12.660
why Driver decided to join the cast of 65 as it&nbsp;
afforded him something different. At the moment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:16.680
however, it seems as if audiences aren't&nbsp;
buying into this version of the actor.

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:22.620
Another piece of this puzzle is that 65 is an&nbsp;
original property, and not part of a franchise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:28.680
much like Creed III, Avatar: The Way of Water, and&nbsp;
Puss in Boots: The Last Wish. Considering that 65&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:34.380
was created for around $91 million, it appears&nbsp;
as if the film has quite the uphill struggle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:40.440
ahead if it wishes to recoup the invested money.&nbsp;
Perhaps 65 will undergo a massive change of fate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:45.720
but at the moment it looks like it's under&nbsp;
the looming shadow of a cataclysmic asteroid.

